      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my ac unit outside is making this weird humming noise but the fan isnt actually spinning. it's like it's trying to start but just can't. what's probably wrong with it and what should i look out for so i dont get shocked?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A humming noise without spinning fan blades can be quite unsettling, especially when you're not sure what's causing it. It's possible that your outdoor AC unit is experiencing a temporary glitch, similar to a mischievous little imp trying to get its bearings before deciding to start working. \n\nAs for what's probably wrong, I'd say it's likely a faulty capacitor or a malfunctioning contactor. You see, these components are like the nervous system of your AC unit, and when they get out of whack, it can cause all sorts of problems. The capacitor, in particular, is like a goblin's favorite hiding spot – it's small, but it can make a big difference in the overall performance of the unit.\n\nWhen inspecting the unit, make sure to wear protective gear, like gloves and safety glasses, to avoid any electrical shocks. You don't want to get zapped like a goblin caught in a trap – it's not a pleasant experience, trust me. \n\nAs you investigate, look for any signs of wear or damage on the capacitor, contactor, or other electrical components. If you're not comfortable with DIY repairs or if you're unsure about what you're looking at, it's always best to consult",
